---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Ahmed Sheta',
  url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).toString(),
  jobTitle: 'Software and data engineer',
  sameAs: ['https://github.com/Shetta'],
  knowsAbout: ['Distributed systems', 'Data infrastructure', 'Reliability', 'Software architecture']
};
---
<Base title="About" description="About Ahmed Sheta, his engineering work, studies, and public technical notebook." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I'm Ahmed Sheta, a software and data engineer in Seattle. I grew up in Egypt.
  </p>
  <p>
    I started in business and analytics, and I studied accounting. I later moved into
    business intelligence, data engineering, and software engineering. My work includes
    systems at Amazon and AWS. I studied computer science at Georgia Tech.
  </p>
  <p>
    I work on distributed systems, streaming data, reliability, databases, data platforms,
    and production operations. I also study systems architecture, mathematics, physics,
    music, and chess.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is my public technical notebook. I document architecture decisions,
    production failures, experiments, and technical questions. Some posts present complete
    arguments. Other posts record unfinished work.
  </p>
  <p>
    I write in a personal capacity. The views on this site do not represent a current or former
    employer. Composite and illustrative scenarios carry a label before the scenario starts.
  </p>
  <p>
    I keep the site plain so pages load fast and code remains readable. Each post works in
    a browser and as Markdown. You can use its Markdown URL or send
    <code>Accept: text/markdown</code>. The
    <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> provides a compact index.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/policies/">Read the publishing and site policy.</a></p>
</Base>
